date: 2026-06-06T22:12:21-04:00
---

The Sin and Tonic is a bar in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]. Owned by [[Illmari Vaino]], it's the current headquarters of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]].

The interior is dingy and dark, and Illmari keeps incense censors burning tobacco hanging from the ceiling during operating ours. The main serving area is a large rectangular room with booths along the walls and a bar in the center. The left exit leads to the workshop and garage, the right exit leads to the stockroom and armory, and the back exit leads to bedrooms and an office.

Unlike many a Fane — its walls sustained by a [[Hearts|Heart]] rather than mere brickwork — the [[Sin and Tonic]] makes no pretence of grandeur: the sleeping quarters are tucked at the back on the same level as the bar, the beds hovering somewhere around two-star comfort on a generous night. The [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|twins]] are the greater draw for those in need, skilled enough to brew healing potions, though they run nothing so formal as a shop — bring your own components, or don't bother asking. A supermarket a few blocks off covers the more mundane resupply.

The bar's staff take messages for the household, faxes included, and the office at the back has a phone.

The garage once held a radar dish taken from the roof of a roller rink. The twins traced it to [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]], with its signal originating from a [[Org/Gryphonline/index|Gryphonline]] distribution center. The [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]] has since taken the dish for its investigation. A small arcane device that came with it, the [[Sentience Distributor]], spreads whatever signal the dish receives; it is fragile, and the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|twins]] advise against switching it on indoors.

The group's company car is called the day tripper, and members can sign it out of the garage in the alley. The [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] took it from outside the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]] and kept it on a hoist in a bay of a [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] auto body shop on Anchor Boulevard in Widdershins; the Party has its keys. The Party's own car is a black Aventine taken from the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]], registered legally under [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] through [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]].

The paintings carried out of [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]]'s manor sit in the armory with [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Elias Ramsey|Elias]].

Keystone 14 is hidden in a small lead-lined safe set in cement under the floor of the room [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] share, since the twins are the most intimidating of the household. The cement comes as quicklime fished out of the river and patted down, and [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]] will not sell it. [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] chose lead because lead or running water stops an ordinary locating spell, though neither would stop a caster who names the stone directly.
